### Axum Item CRUD API — request collection
### Works with the "REST Client" extension in VS Code, JetBrains' built-in
### HTTP client, or any tool that understands the .http format.
###
### Run the server first: `cargo run` (needs Postgres reachable at
### DATABASE_URL — see docker-compose.yml) or `docker compose up`
### (listens on http://localhost:3000)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. List all items (should be empty on a fresh database)
### -----------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/items


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Create an item
### -----------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Widget",
  "description": "A small widget",
  "quantity": 10
}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Create a second item (no description, to check the optional field)
### -----------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Gadget",
  "quantity": 3
}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. List all items again — should show both items now
### -----------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/items


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Get a single item by id
### Change the id below to match one returned from step 2 or 3.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/items/1


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Get an item that doesn't exist — should return 404
### -----------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/items/9999


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. Partially update an item — only quantity changes
### -----------------------------------------------------------------
PUT {{baseUrl}}/items/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 25
}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 8. Fully update an item — all fields provided
### -----------------------------------------------------------------
PUT {{baseUrl}}/items/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Widget Pro",
  "description": "An upgraded widget",
  "quantity": 50
}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 9. Update an item that doesn't exist — should return 404
### -----------------------------------------------------------------
PUT {{baseUrl}}/items/9999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 1
}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 10. Delete an item — should return 204 No Content
### -----------------------------------------------------------------
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/items/2


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 11. Confirm it's gone — should return 404
### -----------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/items/2


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 12. Delete an item that doesn't exist — should return 404
### -----------------------------------------------------------------
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/items/9999


### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 13. Malformed body — missing required "name" field, should 400
### -----------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 5
}
